==Battleground==
*1 [[Scissoroo]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*5 [[Shibalien]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 5.33~14.67 seconds<sup>160f~440f</sup>.
*3 [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn after 24 seconds<sup>720f</sup>, delay 24 seconds<sup>720f</sup>.
*1 [[Helmut Krabbe]] spawns after 32 seconds<sup>960f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Possessed King Doge]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Shibalien]]s spawn, delay 10.67~29.33 seconds<sup>320f~880f</sup>.
**5 [[Mistress Celeboodle]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 24~32 seconds<sup>720f~960f</sup>.
**2 [[Cyberhorn]]s spawn, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
**2 [[Ursamajor]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
**4 [[Helmut Krabbe]]s spawn, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Due to the high number of Alien enemies, [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] are a must. The limited number of enemies means a war of attrition approach will deplete King Doge's support and leave him vulnerable to hits from attackers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]. King Doge's attacks have a long windup, so intelligently using the Cat Cannon to interrupt his attacks will buy your frontline more time.

